1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:00,670
Hi there.

2
00:00:01,190 --> 00:00:05,150
Let's talk about SDLC.

3
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,160
What is it?

4
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:10,880
What stages or steps does it have?

5
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:15,620
And let's practice using passive voice in English.

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:16,700
Let's go.

7
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:24,950
SDLC stands for Software Development Life Cycle.

8
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:31,040
It's a set of steps needed to create software applications.

9
00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:40,580
These steps divide the development process into tasks that can be assigned, completed and measured.

10
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:41,750
Okay.

11
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:46,160
So these are steps of SDLC.

12
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:50,690
First is planning and requirement analysis.

13
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:55,070
Then we have design coding.

14
00:00:55,460 --> 00:01:00,090
Testing, deployment and maintenance.

15
00:01:00,090 --> 00:01:04,260
Let's have a closer look at each of the steps.

16
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:08,490
So first requirement analysis and planning.

17
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:18,960
This is about planning the work on the project, calculating time needed and number of people in a team.

18
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:28,020
Requirement analysis is to define what the application is supposed to do and how people can use it.

19
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:36,870
For example, if you develop a social media application, you would need it to be able to connect people

20
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:39,300
and send messages.

21
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:42,660
So these are the main requirements for them.

22
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,940
Social media applications.

23
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:48,750
Then we have a design stage.

24
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:55,830
Business architects use the requirements to produce several designs of the product.

25
00:01:55,860 --> 00:02:00,000
Prototyping can be a part of this phase.

26
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:05,630
A prototype is like one of the early versions of software.

27
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,260
All right, then.

28
00:02:08,270 --> 00:02:16,130
Coding design documents are used to implement the design and produce the code.

29
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:20,480
This stage is the longest stage of SDLC.

30
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:33,580
Testing code is tested based on the climate requirements to ensure the code works according to specifications.

31
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:41,470
The testing phase helps to reduce the number of bugs and glitches that users might have.

32
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,920
Deployment.

33
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:52,840
The product is delivered to the customers, so now application can be used by users.

34
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,860
Great.

35
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:55,840
Okay.

36
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,760
Maintenance then.

37
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:06,130
User experiences technical issues with the product and it requires support and fixes.

38
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:08,740
That is a maintenance stage.

39
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,210
Okay.

40
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:19,750
I used this sentences design documents are used to implement the design and produce the code.

41
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:29,770
Code is tested based on the client requirements to ensure the code works according to specifications.

42
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:33,940
The product is delivered to the customer.

43
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:37,090
Have a look at this sentences.

44
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,540
Do we know who does the action?

45
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,600
No, we don't.

46
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:46,550
And in this case we used passive voice.

47
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:49,490
How to make passive Voice.

48
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:00,050
Let's have a look at active sentence in present Simple team uses design documents to implement design

49
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:02,090
and produce code.

50
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,250
Okay, we know that subject.

51
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,930
Here is team.

52
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:13,250
Now we avoid the word team and we make a passive sentence.

53
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:21,230
Design documents are used to implement the design and produce the code.

54
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:28,790
So in passive voice we used the verb to be in the correct form.

55
00:04:29,450 --> 00:04:34,500
Ah, in this case, and we used past participle.

56
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:38,210
So past participle is the verb.

57
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:44,560
Plus ending ed for regular verbs and for irregular verbs.

58
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:49,920
You need to check the third column of the table of irregular verbs.

59
00:04:50,010 --> 00:04:54,630
Okay, use is regular, so we just add it.

60
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:55,080
Ed?

61
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:07,580
Okay, Here we have an active sentence in past tense team delivered product to the customer.

62
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:12,500
So in passive we need to use past as well.

63
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:17,150
The product was delivered to the customer.

64
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:21,770
So was it's the verb to be in the past.

65
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:23,890
All right.

66
00:05:23,930 --> 00:05:27,230
Why do we need to use passive voice?

67
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:28,610
Case.

68
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:33,370
One, we don't know who does or did the action.

69
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:34,990
We don't know the subject.

70
00:05:34,990 --> 00:05:38,650
For example, painting was stolen.

71
00:05:38,650 --> 00:05:40,630
We don't know who stole it.

72
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:45,430
Second case, the subject is not important.

73
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:49,090
She was invited to the interview.

74
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:53,190
We don't know or we don't care who invited her.

75
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:57,550
We are interested in the fact that she was invited.

76
00:05:57,850 --> 00:06:04,120
And next case, we don't want to focus on who made a mistake.

77
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:08,080
For example, deadline was missed here.

78
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:15,970
The focus is on the fact that deadline was missed, but not on who missed the deadline.

79
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,500
All right.

80
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,170
Good.

81
00:06:18,190 --> 00:06:20,860
Go to your file and do the tasks.

82
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:24,400
If you need to refresh your memory, come back to the video.

83
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:26,260
Thank you and see you.

84
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:26,650
Bye.
